1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,458
CHAPTER 5 — THE WHITE CITY

2
00:00:03,808 --> 00:00:12,577
In 1893, Chicago hosted a World's Fair. It was going to be the first ever lit entirely by electricity.

3
00:00:12,777 --> 00:00:19,546
Westinghouse won the contract: he offered to do it with alternating current for far less than Edison's camp.

4
00:00:19,746 --> 00:00:26,593
On opening day, the president pressed a button… and about a hundred thousand lamps lit up.

5
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:33,716
Inside the Electricity Building, crowds gathered in front of a giant copper egg. It spun all by itself.

6
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:40,916
A few years later, his system carried power from Niagara Falls to Buffalo, over twenty miles away.

7
00:00:41,116 --> 00:00:48,423
But the war left Westinghouse buried in debt. His bankers wanted to eliminate Tesla's two dollars and fifty cents.

8
00:00:48,623 --> 00:00:54,316
The most famous version says Tesla tore up the contract right in front of him, out of friendship.

9
00:00:54,516 --> 00:01:03,670
The documents tell a less theatrical story: he gave up his royalties and later sold his patents for about two hundred and sixteen thousand dollars.

10
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:09,877
His system conquered the world. And he no longer collected a cent from it.
